## 3. The cross-CTA `grid.sync` usage you REPLACE — and the `G=1` reduction

The grid barrier is the **`MCTA_BARRIER()` macro, defined lines 361–382**, invoked at lines **421, 468, 518**. It is *not* `cooperative_groups::grid.sync()` — it is a hand-rolled per-matrix **sense-reversal barrier** over the `G` CTAs of one matrix, using `bar_cnt[bid]` / `bar_sense[bid]` and `st.release.gpu`/`ld.acquire.gpu` PTX:

```c
#define MCTA_BARRIER() do {                                            \
    __syncthreads();                                                   \
    if (tid == 0) {                                                    \
        __threadfence();                                               \
        int my = priv_sense ^ 1; priv_sense = my;                      \
        if (atomicAdd(bcnt, 1) == G - 1) {                             \
            atomicExch(bcnt, 0);                                       \
            asm volatile("st.release.gpu.b32 [%0], %1;" :: "l"(bsen), "r"(my) : "memory"); \
        } else {                                                       \
            int seen;                                                  \
            do { asm volatile("ld.acquire.gpu.b32 %0, [%1];" : "=r"(seen) : "l"(bsen) : "memory"); } \
            while (seen != my);                                        \
        }                                                              \
    }                                                                  \
    __syncthreads();                                                   \
} while (0)
```

